adjudication.rationale:
In the new `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts` handler, the webhook auth check is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is not set (i.e., `undefined`) and the request omits that header (so the header lookup also yields `undefined`), then the comparison is `undefined !== undefined`, which is `false`, so the request is treated as authenticated and proceeds to credential update/create.

The diff does not include any additional guard like “reject if secret is unset”, so this is a real auth-bypass risk when the endpoint is deployed with credential sharing enabled but without configuring the secret.
